From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:00:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bus: don't free a caller-owned range array on static BAR1
 fallback

kbusGetStaticFbAperture_TU102() frees pMemArea->pRanges whenever
kbusIncreaseStaticBar1Refcount() fails, including the NV_ERR_IN_USE and
NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED cases that just fall back to a dynamic mapping. With
BUS_MAP_FB_FLAGS_UNMANAGED_MEM_AREA the array is not allocated here: it
belongs to the caller, and kbusMapFbApertureSingle() passes a MemoryRange on
its stack. A kernel-internal BAR1 mapping (memdescMap, context DMA, kernel
mappings of virtual memory, USERD) of FB memory with a non-default kind and
sub-2MB pages, a CPU-cached memdesc, or a kind that conflicts with an existing
static reference therefore frees a stack address and then continues with the
dynamic mapping into that same array.

Only free the array when this function allocated it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../gpu/bus/arch/turing/kern_bus_tu102.c      | 24 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/turing/kern_bus_tu102.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/turing/kern_bus_tu102.c
index da0700c3..61bc4302 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/turing/kern_bus_tu102.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/arch/turing/kern_bus_tu102.c
@@ -1189,18 +1189,28 @@ kbusGetStaticFbAperture_TU102
 
     status = kbusIncreaseStaticBar1Refcount_HAL(pGpu, pKernelBus, pMemDesc, busMapFlags);
 
-    if (status == NV_ERR_IN_USE || status == NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED)
+    if (status != NV_OK)
     {
+        //
+        // An unmanaged range array belongs to the caller (it is on the
+        // stack in kbusMapFbApertureSingle), only free what was allocated
+        // above.
+        //
+        if (!bUnmanagedRange)
+        {
+            portMemFree(pMemArea->pRanges);
+            pMemArea->pRanges = NULL;
+        }
+
         //
         // This mapping is already in use or not supported,
         // and we need to make a dynamic mapping instead
         //
-        portMemFree(pMemArea->pRanges);
-        return NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
-    }
-    else if (status != NV_OK)
-    {
-        portMemFree(pMemArea->pRanges);
+        if (status == NV_ERR_IN_USE || status == NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED)
+        {
+            return NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+        }
+
         return status;
     }
 
